{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe Rhine at Cologne is a different beast from the stream near Berlin. The river is wide, grey, and swollen with commerce. I counted twelve large two-masted vessels today, each one a testament to the practical spirit of the West. I walked the streets, the air thick with the smell of fish and coal smoke.\n\nI visited the cathedral; the interior is impressive, though the light is gloomy. I am to attend mass tomorrow morning with the young Counts Stolberg and their tutor, Dean Kellermann. Kellermann speaks with the confidence of a man who has never been contradicted. He believes the constitution grows from the soil, not from Parisian pamphlets. I am to leave for Aachen this afternoon. The innkeeper charged me two thalers for a room that smells of damp wool and yesterday’s onions.\n\nI hope Karl is doing well in his studies. Obedience is the first lesson; I miss seeing him learn to listen before he speaks.\n\nYour affectionate,\nG.W.F.H."}}],"created":1795219287,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":218,"prompt_tokens":1113,"total_tokens":1331,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-sAeTVTzJeoJXqolpUmIeHeUGZMA8jxJG","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1113,"prompt_ms":1074.706,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9655938903863431,"prompt_per_second":1035.6320705383614,"predicted_n":218,"predicted_ms":5130.617,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.643396313364057,"predicted_per_second":42.29510797629213}}